Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-ecm: fix wifi event bind call for Linux 6.18

Linux 6.18 reworked the in-kernel sockaddr handling and changed the
struct proto_ops bind() callback prototype to take a
"struct sockaddr_unsized *" pointer instead of "struct sockaddr *"
(commit "net: Convert proto_ops bind() callbacks to use sockaddr_unsized").
Cast the netlink address accordingly when calling sock->ops->bind()
directly from the wifi event thread.

---
--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -8209,7 +8209,11 @@ static void ecm_interface_wifi_event_thr
 	saddr.nl_groups = RTNLGRP_LINK;
 	saddr.nl_pid    = current->pid;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 18, 0)
+	err = __ewn.sock->ops->bind(__ewn.sock, (struct sockaddr_unsized *)&saddr, sizeof(struct sockaddr));
+#else
 	err = __ewn.sock->ops->bind(__ewn.sock, (struct sockaddr *)&saddr, sizeof(struct sockaddr));
+#endif
 	if (err < 0) {
 		DEBUG_ERROR("failed to bind sock\n");
 		goto exit2;
